Vitamin B12 is a nutrient that helps keep the body's nerve and blood cells healthy and helps make DNA, the genetic material in all cells (https://www.ruh.nhs.uk/patients/patient_information/PAE146_Vitamin_B12.pdf). It is naturally found in animal products such as meat, fish, seafood, poultry, eggs, milk, yogurt and cheese, and is also added to fortified plant‑based products and meat substitutes (https://www.tyntesfield.nhs.uk/vitamin-b12-and-diet). The UK recommended daily intake for adults aged 19 to 64 is about 1.5 micrograms (https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/vitamin-b).

